- K4. `Project(project_id, employee_id)`, `Employee(employee_id, name, experience_years)` — average experience per project.


select p.project_id ,AVG(e.experience_years) as avg_exp
from employee e
join project p
on p.employee_id = e.employee_id
group by p.project_id;


5. Departments with more than 3 employees, showing department name (JOIN + GROUP BY + HAVING combined).

`Employee(id, name, salary, department_id)`, `Department(id, name)


select d.name
from department d
join employee e
on e.department_id= d.id
group by d.name
having count(distinct e.id) >3;


